※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4104 LANG_IMPORT_NOT_EXPORTED

※ A bundle without `@[export]` is the file's own, and applying one is refused
※ for the reason it is refused of everything else a module keeps.
※
※ It is told apart from a name the module does not have at all: the module keeps
※ every bundle it wrote, and which of the two it is decides what the message
※ says -- "not yours to apply" and "there is no such thing" being two different
※ things for a reader to do something about.

let private := ⎕import("private")

fn smaller(a: T', b: T') → T' pre(private.secret(T')):
    a ⌊ b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(smaller(2u8, 3u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
